After ascending my first attempt on a fresh install on a new computer,
I decided it was time to try some conducts. I had several failed
attempts to do ascend a pacifist monk. Many I quit
after a bump kill. A few died after being overwelmed by monsters on
the way to
the protection racket. I decided to try again and died in a most
unexpected way.

I started with a little dog named spike. He happily killed and ate
many
monsters and helped steal & credit clone from 2 shops before the
Gnomish mines.
Spike also helped me decide a ring mail was safe to wear making bump
kills
much less of a possibility. When I got to the mines I credit cloned
one shop
and spike was good at killing gaurds but that watch captain made me
nervous.
I bought protection and found a good split mail to switch with my ring
mail. I
also found a cream pie, yah! So now my AC was -15 and I decided to
credit
clone the general store. Unfortunately the watchman came close and
Spike
attacked. Poor little Spike killed by the watchman. Poor me with my
bag of
stuff in the shop grrr.

So Now I'm a petless pacifist. I went up and down levels using the E
word
over and over again to make my way through tight spots. I dropped
enough
junk in the general shop to get a 600z and went to the Oracle to level
up.
I also made sure I had a nice pile of food with the rest of my credit.

Unfortuneatey the oracle had a werejackle who managed to make that
level
rather full of crappy little adversaries. I still mangaged to get up
to level 3.
Now i spent an endless amount of time trying to get a new pet going.
For a while
a kitten joined me in minetown. I didn't even get a chance to name her
before a
dwarf burrowed through the wall and killed her while i was protecting
her. I
also had a kitten one level below minetown killed by another horde.
In
desperation I took off a split mail and let the werejackle on the
oracle level
infect me. Unfortuneatly, the one pet jackle I got was quite a wimp :p
Some
wolfsbane took care of my furry problem. I tried to tame a dog with a
food
ration but strangely it just made him friendly. I guess dogs don't
like food.

I also learned how to use traps to help clear levels. Except a
polytrap
I foolishly stepped into turning into a master mind flayer. I
carefully
flew around for a while and didn't attack anything. Eventually, I
found several
rings. I price ID the 200 level ones and took them to a sink. Luckly
I found a ring of SD. Now all I need is conflict to help clear these
levels so
I can hopefully raise a happy pet. At some point my cream pie
disappeared,
maybe it served it's purpose. I'll have to be more careful.

I had a brilliant idea to alter scum and hopefully get a spellbook of
charm monster and sleep. Unfortunately, apparently my god is mad at
me.
Another consequence of my gods anger it took me a little while to
notice is
that I lost all intrinsic protection. This led me to wonder if I
absent mindly
tried to engrave on an alter.

I decided to dive further and maybe hopefully get a wish. It seemed
like a
wish or conflict was my only chance at this point. A couple levels
under the
oracle the RNG decided to smile uppon me and a kitten I named Bjorn
approached.
With my stethescope I monitored Bjorns progress. Together we cleared
the
oracle hord and made a puppy friend Lupe and a pony friend Prancer in
the
progress. Things are starting to look good again.

Taking them back down the mines time to clear minetown, buy some
protection
and try to appease my god. Unfortunately Prancer had a run in with my
coaligned priest and fed Bjorn. Once I cleared the level and
credit clone / protection racketed myself back to AC -15 I decided to
dive further to hopefully polymorph some pets. I only found 1
polymorph trap
before the mines end and unfortunately found it by stepping in. I was
lucky I
polymorphed into something that didn't destroy my armor but on the
other hand
an imp is really quite useless. I used a crude dagger trown to the
ceiling to
bring myself back to my senses. I also made friends with a warhorse on
the way
down. When I descended into the mines end without my pets,
just to check it out, two vampires followed me back up and drained my
pets so
they wouldn't attack. I took them down to the mines end hoping to find
a
polytrap in the initial room & get some beafier pets. No polytrap in
the
initial room and Bjorn and the warhorse died from a boulder trap /
ettin mummy.
Disappointed, I decided to go back up and leave this crap behind till
I can
get some better pets. We skipped merrily past the vampires and
happened to
find a couple unicorns on the way up. Finally a unicorn horn. Now I
can
more-safely quaff some potions. The potions gave me 2-gain level and
3 gain energy along with a few extra healing to beaf up those HP. In
minetown
I found a new housecat I named Scoan. Still no magic whistle,
I have a leash and a tin one tho. I also price IDed some spellbooks to
find a
level one spellbook, what luck sleep. Unfortunately can't do much with
that
till I get some better armor.

So time to try Sokoban. The helm of telepathy I had mad navigating
the
boulders with pets much easier. On the way up I found a wand of
polymorph
which I stashed for later. After my pets had cleared the final room I
found an amulet of reflection. That's good cause I already found
2 bags of holding and a wand. When engrave testing the wand I get my
first
wish. I wished for 2 blessed scrolls of charging and get 1. I zap the
wand
and wish for a blessed +2 silver dragon scale mail and get it.
I swapped the spell inhibiting elven mithril coat for the lighter
better dragon scale mail. Okay my gods still angry with me but things
are really
looking up at this point. I hold off wishing for a figurine of
archon,
my last ascension my would be pet archon attacked me. I def need some
better
pets but think i might be better off with a spellbook of charm
monster. For
now I wait and practice the sleep spell. Now AC=-20.

At minetown I decided to burn the rest of my wishes for some nice
spellbooks.
I got charm monster, healing and create monster and the Mitre of
Holiness to
help with spellcasting and energy.

Maybe I should have wished
for a magic whistle instead, but this growing pile on unicorn horns in
my
bag of holding & my wand of polymorph says otherwise. When I got to
the mines
end I abandoned my regular pets and tamed the Vampires who had killed
my other
pets. They quickly became Vampire Lords and besides feeling weary all
the time
were good friends to me.

Going back to the main dungeon I stole from a shopkeeper using a
scroll of
teleportation to take a worthless piece of armor. I would have paid
the
shopkeeper for it, but my V lords had other plans for him. So now I
have a
nice pile of cream pies to weild just in case. Though, I only used my
previous cream pie by accidentally applying it. Body armor makes
keeping
pacifist conduct for a monk much easier.

I found a level with an alter I converted and
started using my stethescope on monsters to try to find some toughies
to
appease my god. Unfortuneatly, one of my level 18 vampire lords found
a
polytrap on the opposite end of the level and turned into a level 9
tengu :p

This got the gears turning. I locked my Vampire Lord out of the
polytrap room
and started creating monsters. The first usefull one was a
disenchanter. I
quickly led him to my vampire lord. Unfortuneately, the corpse wasn't
viable
after dragging across the level. So again I locked my V's out and
created
monsters. A scary moment came when I created another vampire lord.
I can't afford level drain with the quest coming up. Thankfully he
was
charmed by my charm monster spell. I locked him out of the room as
well and
started creating monsters again.
A zurty looks appropriate. So I leashed one of my V's and carfully
lured the
zurty towards the alter. Thankfully the zurty corpse molified my god.
On my first sacrifice after getting on the good side again I was given
a
The Sunsword. A sacrificed again till it was safe to pray and made
some holy
water.

I dove farther down with my V lords and found the quest. Since I was
only
@ level 6 I can't do it yet. I had one very scary moment. One of the
poly
traps on the level created an air elemental. I tried taming twice,
one time I failed cause of my elven shield. I tried zapping with a
wand of polymorph with no affect (maybe the wand is dead).
I was pummelled with debris down to 2HP before I was able to zap with
a
wand of teleportation. Why I decided to waste a polymorph charge over
a
teleportation charge is beyond me.

After trying to get all my pets out of the Quest. I had made a few new
friends
here I went to work. When I came home I went to bed a toothache woke
me and
I decided to play a little more. I opened a terminal and typed in
nethack.
It told me a game was in progress.
"Do you want to destroy the current game (y/n)?". I hit n a few times
with no
response. So I hit cntrl-c with no response.
So I closed the terminal window and found the other terminal to start
playing.
When I went back to the quest level it said something was missing and
I died of trickery. The devteam thinks of everything. So much for my
most
promising pacifist game ever. YASD :p


